§ `Regulations 45(10H) and 45ZA(6) as obligations with a deadline (MUST ... WITHIN 90): traces, read by hand`

-- A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with #ASSERT on the main binary, so these traces are READ, not asserted.  Expected from the text
-- ("within 90 days"): notifying at time 90 or earlier is FULFILLED; at time 91, or never, is a BREACH.  The decision functions above
-- (`... was given within 90 days`) are asserted with the same boundary.
#TRACE `reg 45(10H) the trustees must notify the Commissioners within 90 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 45(10H) the trustees of a taxable relevant trust` DOES `reg 45(10H) notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred` AT 90

#TRACE `reg 45(10H) the trustees must notify the Commissioners within 90 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 45(10H) the trustees of a taxable relevant trust` DOES `reg 45(10H) notify the Commissioners of the change and the date on which it occurred` AT 91

#TRACE `reg 45ZA(6) the trustee must notify the Commissioners within 90 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 45ZA(6) a trustee of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies` DOES `reg 45ZA(6) notify the Commissioners of the change` AT 90

#TRACE `reg 45ZA(6) the trustee must notify the Commissioners within 90 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 45ZA(6) a trustee of a trust to which paragraph (1) applies` DOES `reg 45ZA(6) notify the Commissioners of the change` AT 91
